### Documentation Angle

Write this as a **marketplace web system design** with user roles, subscription workflow, vehicle listing schema, payment flow, admin moderation, security, commission model and deployment plan.', '', '', '', '/docs/automarketpro-car-marketplace.pdf', 'In Progress', 'Full-Stack Developer', '2026', false, true, 8, null),
  ('unity-fps-sniper-contracts-prototype', 'Unity FPS Sniper Contracts Prototype', 'A tactical FPS sniper prototype with AI states, missions, vehicles, weapons, ADS and large terrain design.', 'Game Development', array['Unity', 'C#', 'AI', 'Level Design', 'Blender', 'AI Systems', 'Vehicle Controller']::text[], '/img/projects/unity-fps-sniper-contracts-prototype.webp', array['/img/projects/tactical-fps.webp']::text[], '### Project Description

Unity FPS Sniper Contracts Prototype is a tactical first-person shooter game prototype inspired by mission-based sniper gameplay. It includes a large playable environment, mission objectives, AI patrol/combat states, weapon mechanics, scope overlays, vehicle systems and player interaction logic. Unity’s execution model and event function lifecycle are important when documenting systems such as Update, FixedUpdate, physics, input, animation and AI behaviour.

### Problem

Building a tactical FPS requires coordinating multiple gameplay systems: player controller, weapon firing, AI state machines, mission objectives, vehicles, UI, physics and level design. If these systems are not modular, the project becomes difficult to scale.

### Solution

The project is structured as a modular prototype where each major gameplay function is separated into systems: weapon system, mission manager, AI controller, vehicle controller, scope UI and game manager.

### Main Features

