### Documentation Angle

Document this as a **game systems engineering case study**. Include gameplay architecture, AI state diagram, weapon flow diagram, vehicle physics logic, mission sequence and future level roadmap.', '', 'https://github.com/MuhammadHaiderAbbas/TacticalFPS-Unity', '', '/docs/unity-fps-sniper-contracts-prototype.pdf', 'Prototype', 'Game Developer', '2026', false, true, 9, null),
  ('dvwa-ethical-hacking-labs', 'Cybersecurity DVWA & Ethical Hacking Labs', 'Hands-on cybersecurity labs using DVWA, Burp Suite, OWASP concepts and professional reporting practice.', 'Cybersecurity', array['DVWA', 'Burp Suite', 'OWASP', 'Security', 'OWASP testing workflow']::text[], '/img/projects/dvwa-ethical-hacking-labs.webp', array['/img/projects/dvwa-01.webp', '/img/projects/dvwa-02.webp', '/img/projects/dvwa-03.webp', '/img/projects/dvwa-04.webp', '/img/projects/dvwa-05.webp', '/img/projects/dvwa-06.webp', '/img/projects/dvwa-07.webp']::text[], '### Project Description

This project is a controlled ethical hacking lab using DVWA and related web security tools to practise vulnerability discovery, exploitation and remediation. DVWA is a deliberately vulnerable web application designed for legal security training. OWASP Top 10 provides a widely recognised framework for common web application security risks, and Burp Suite is a common tool for web penetration testing.

### Problem

Students and junior security professionals need a safe environment to practise security testing without attacking real systems. Real websites cannot be tested without permission, so controlled labs are essential.

### Solution

The lab uses intentionally vulnerable applications to practise SQL injection, XSS, CSRF, brute force, insecure upload, weak authentication and other common vulnerabilities. Each test can be documented with vulnerability description, impact, evidence and remediation.

### Main Features / Lab Areas

Lab AreaLearning Outcome

SQL Injection

Understand database query manipulation

XSS

Understand client-side script injection

CSRF

Understand unauthorised request execution

Brute Force

Understand weak login protection

File Upload

Understand unsafe upload risks

Security Levels

Compare low, medium and high defences

Reporting

Write professional vulnerability reports

### Documentation Angle

This should become a **cybersecurity lab report pack** with each vulnerability documented as: objective, setup, method, evidence, risk rating, mitigation and reflection.', '', '', '', '/docs/dvwa-ethical-hacking-labs.pdf', 'Practical Labs', 'Security Learner', '2026', false, true, 10, null),
  ('jarvis-ai-agent-workflow', 'Jarvis AI Agent Workflow', 'A modular AI assistant workflow concept using n8n-style automation, local models and API actions.', 'AI / Automation', array['AI Agents', 'n8n', 'Ollama', 'Automation', 'Prompting', 'APIs']::text[], '/img/projects/jarvis-ai-agent-workflow.webp', '{}'::text[], '### Project Description

Jarvis AI Agent Workflow is a modular AI assistant concept designed to automate personal or business tasks using workflow orchestration. The system can combine triggers, actions, LLM reasoning, APIs, local models and user commands. n8n is relevant because it supports workflow automation and AI-agent style tool orchestration, while Ollama supports running local language models on a user machine.

### Problem

Users often repeat the same tasks across emails, calendars, notes, web searches, reminders, project planning and file organisation. Doing everything manually wastes time and creates fragmented workflows.

### Solution

The Jarvis workflow connects different tools into one automation layer. A user command can trigger a chain of actions such as reading data, summarising content, creating tasks, generating emails, updating spreadsheets or calling APIs.

### Main Features

FeatureDescription

Command Input

User sends task/request

Agent Router

Decides what workflow to trigger

n8n Workflow

Automates actions between tools

Local AI Model

Runs private local reasoning through Ollama

API Integrations

Connects email, calendar, docs, websites

Memory Layer

Stores user preferences or project notes

Notification System

Sends final result or alert

### Documentation Angle

Write this as an **AI workflow automation architecture**. Include agent workflow diagram, tool-calling pipeline, privacy design, local vs cloud AI comparison and example use cases.', '', '', '', '/docs/jarvis-ai-agent-workflow.pdf', 'Concept / Prototype', 'Automation Designer', '2026', false, true, 11, null),
  ('full-stack-dating-app-prototype', 'Full-Stack Dating App Prototype', 'A full-stack app prototype with authentication direction, profile flow, matching concept and database schema planning.', 'Web Systems', array['React', 'Node', 'Prisma', 'PostgreSQL', 'Node.js']::text[], '/img/projects/full-stack-dating-app-prototype.webp', '{}'::text[], '### Project Description

The Full-Stack Dating App Prototype is a modern dating platform concept with user registration, authentication, profile creation, matching logic, messaging flow and backend APIs. React is suitable for building interactive user interfaces, Node.js supports backend JavaScript runtime execution, Prisma provides modern ORM/database access, and PostgreSQL supports relational data modelling.

