### Value to a company

For employers, this supports roles requiring trust, calm customer interaction, premises safety and clear incident reporting. It proves I can operate responsibly around the public, follow instructions, protect people and escalate risks without creating unnecessary conflict.

### Practical use

Useful in retail, hotels, events, corporate sites and any environment where people, assets and access points must be monitored professionally.', '', '/img/certs/sia-door-supervisor-license.webp', 1, true),
  ('Certified Ethical Hacker — CEH', 'EC-Council', '2023', 'Ethical hacking methodology, reconnaissance, vulnerability concepts, tools and defensive awareness.', '### What I learnt

CEH strengthened my understanding of the ethical hacking lifecycle: reconnaissance, scanning, vulnerability discovery, system and web application attack concepts, wireless/cloud awareness, cryptography basics, documentation and defensive thinking. The learning is not only about tools; it is about understanding attacker behaviour so weaknesses can be found and fixed responsibly.

### Value to a company

Companies benefit from this because it supports secure-development thinking, vulnerability awareness, better testing conversations and stronger risk reporting. It helps bridge the gap between developers, IT teams and security staff when building or reviewing systems.

### Practical use

Useful for web application security reviews, OWASP-style testing, vulnerability documentation, risk assessment, security lab work and defensive improvement planning.', '', '/img/certs/certified-ethical-hacker-ceh.webp', 2, true),
  ('CompTIA Security+ SY0-601', 'CompTIA', '', 'Risk management, threats, incident response, architecture, cryptography and security operations.', '### What I learnt

Security+ develops broad cybersecurity fundamentals across threats, attacks, vulnerabilities, secure architecture, implementation, operations, incident response, governance, risk and compliance. It is a strong foundation for understanding how security controls protect networks, applications, devices and data.

### Value to a company

For a company, this shows I understand practical security language and can support safer system design, access control, incident awareness, risk discussions and basic security operations. It is valuable in IT support, junior cybersecurity, cloud, web development and technical analyst roles.

### Practical use

Useful for secure configuration awareness, incident triage, risk registers, authentication/authorization planning, cloud security discussions and compliance-minded documentation.', '', '/img/certs/comptia-security-sy0-601.webp', 3, true),
  ('Cyber Security: Understand Threats and Prevent Attacks', 'Online Certification', '', 'Foundational security learning focused on common threats, prevention strategies and secure digital behaviour.', '### What I learnt

This certification focuses on recognizing common cyber threats, understanding how attackers exploit weak behaviour or weak systems, and applying prevention habits such as strong access control, awareness, updates, backups and safer digital workflows.

### Value to a company

It supports company readiness by improving security awareness, reducing avoidable mistakes and helping teams understand why policies, training and basic controls matter.

### Practical use

Useful for staff awareness, secure daily operations, phishing-risk reduction, policy communication and entry-level cybersecurity support.', '', '/img/certs/cyber-security-understand-threats-and-prevent-attacks.webp', 4, true),
  ('Introduction to CISM', 'Security Governance', '', 'Security governance, risk, information security programs and incident management principles.', '### What I learnt

This learning introduced the management side of information security: governance, risk ownership, security program design and incident management. It connects technical controls with business needs, leadership priorities and measurable security improvement.

### Value to a company

Companies need security decisions that align with business value, not only technical tools. This certificate supports communication with management, risk-based prioritisation, policy thinking and structured security program planning.

### Practical use

Useful for risk assessments, security reporting, policy review, compliance discussions, incident-management planning and translating technical issues for non-technical stakeholders.', '', '/img/certs/introduction-to-cism.webp', 5, true),
  ('Ulster MSc Coursework Portfolio', 'Ulster University', '2026', 'Academic evidence across AI, big data, cloud infrastructure, digital transformation and cybersecurity ontology research.', '### What I learnt

The MSc coursework portfolio brings together AI, big data, cloud infrastructure, digital transformation and cybersecurity research. It shows academic planning, technical investigation, written analysis, project design and evidence-based problem solving.

### Value to a company

For employers, this demonstrates postgraduate-level learning, research discipline, documentation quality and the ability to connect modern technologies with practical business and security problems.

### Practical use

Useful for AI projects, cloud/data analysis, technical research, documentation-heavy roles, solution design and graduate-level software or cybersecurity pathways.', '', '/img/certs/ulster-msc-coursework-portfolio.webp', 6, true)
